WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.590
Jeez, don't cry, Nadeshiko.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.580
We can always talk.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.990
Besides, you'll make friends in no time.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.240
I promise I'll come back to hang 
out over winter break, Aya-chan.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.250
I'll come over to your place, too.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.200
So you'd better take care of yourself.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.730
Since you're going somewhere new,
why not try doing something new?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.740
<b>Nishiizu Dining Hall</b>

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:22.450
<b>(2) Episode 12
Izu Camping!!! Birthdays!</b>

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.740
No fair, Rin-chan,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.130
going off on your own to 
freshen up at the hot spring.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.770
You guys were all asleep, and I was bored.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.940
<i>Rinjuvenated.</i>

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.250
<i>Rinfreshed.</i>

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.250
Here you are.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.000
Seafood Bowl

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.660
Be sure to stir it well.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.920
Thank you.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.760
Time to eat!

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.350
It's so good!

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.140
It's like egg on rice, but with seafood.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.820
Sashimi in the morning as we watch the sea...

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.330
How lovely.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.270
It's noon already, Sensei.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:59.510
Aki-chan, we're going straight to camp
 after Dougashima and the tombolo, right?

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.780
Yeah, let's take it slow today.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.710
You sure do eat a lot for being so small.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.540
The tokoroten's good.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:28.810
Dougashima

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.890
<i>Geospot number eight: Dougashima.</i>

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:28.810
<i>Like Sawada Park, it offers a view of 
numerous islands formed from volcanic ash.</i>

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:35.090
Tensodo

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.970
What a huge hole.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.520
Jumping in this water
 must feel great in summer.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.040
You'd probably never come back out.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.580
Sanshiroujima

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.580
<i>Geospot number nine: Sanshiroujima.</i>

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.000
<i>Depending on the angle you view it from, 
you'll see either three or four islands,</i>

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.380
<i>hence the name "Sanshiroujima."</i>

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:59.920
<i>It can be reached on foot during low tide.</i>

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:06.060
Early in the morning, local chefs 
bring supplies across the water by boat,

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.480
and open up food stalls only during 
low tide, when the path is clear.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:16.570
That's where you get the 
gourmet barbecue of Nishiizu...

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.860
the legendary Sanshiroujima Tombolo.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.440
We'll be right there!

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.610
Wait for us, tombolo!

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.250
Can't wait, huh?

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.320
<i>What do we do about this?</i>

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.000
Hey, the tide's slowly going out.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.250
Is it?

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.390
Look. Compare it to this 
picture I took earlier.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.630
Hey, you're right.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.620
Do you think it's about time 
we can cross now, Aki-chan?

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.380
Yeah, let's go.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:48.570
There's no path across the middle part yet.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:51.640
It looks like people are 
starting to cross, though.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.140
Everyone's crossing it for the tombolo!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.170
Hurry! Before they eat it all!

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.900
Let's go, guys!

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.400
Jeez, what can we do?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.540
Sorry I'm late.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.740
I couldn't find a parking spot nearby.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.910
Thanks for coming, Sensei.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.780
We're about to cross the tombolo.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.620
What about you?

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.530
I'll watch from here.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.590
Go ahead, and be safe.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:21.670
Okay.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:23.840
See you!

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.180
The rocks are so loose.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:28.960
It's hard to walk.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.110
It is.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.540
Don't run, you two! You'll fall!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.350
You fell?

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.270
Yeah...

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.200
Hey, Aki...

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.570
You think we might have 
come a bit too early?

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.590
We'll get soaked.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:50.070
Fne. Let's wait a little longer.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.830
Wait, she's already crossing!

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.990
I can't believe I'm in the water in March.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.730
It's really cold!

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.340
I should have brought my sandals.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.780
I know.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.070
I'm on the island!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.030
Is the tombolo stall open now?

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.870
Huh? I don't see the food stall anywhere.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.860
Akari-chan...

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:30.160
A tombolo isn't food.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.990
It's when low tide reveals a path 
between two bodies of land.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.250
You lied to me, Aoi-chan!

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:45.150
Sorry. You were just so enthusiastic 
about the tombolo,

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.010
I couldn't bring myself to tell you.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.740
But you know, it's just 
like cabbage and lettuce.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.510
Cabbage and lettuce?

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.810
You know how some kids have 
a hard time telling them apart?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.950
But as you get older, you learn the difference.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:02.150
Same with the tombolo.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:06.020
I can't believe you know 
that a tombolo isn't...

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.980
You've grown up so much, Akari!

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:11.720
I don't want to grow up!

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.370
I want to eat tombolo!

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.910
<i>What's with these sisters?</i>

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:25.540
I don't think we can make 
it to that other island.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:30.000
Apparently this is as far as you can 
go without getting your feet wet.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.800
They're already soaked.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:36.300
I bet it'd be fun to swim across
 during the summer.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.060
I bet.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.100
Just thinking about it made me cold.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.250
Some other time, huh?

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:45.770
Yeah.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.500
Guys!

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.820
We'd better go back before 
we get caught by the high tide.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.740
Okay, coming!

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:56.070
In an hour, a path emerges from the sea.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.590
And in another hour, 
it vanishes back into the water.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.910
It's a mystery of nature.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.350
Shopping complete!

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.870
Apology for the Tombolo Lie

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:27.860
Sensei, is it all right if I drive in front
 until we get to the campsite?

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:32.490
That's right. You said you wanted 
to ride down the Nishiizu Skyline.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:37.210
Be careful not to get so distracted 
by the scenery that you crash.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:38.120
Okay.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:41.620
Allow me to explain.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:46.630
Shimarin merges with her moped, 
transforming into Perfect Shimarin

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:51.650
and enabling her to travel at a 
whopping 30 kilometers per hour.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.380
Anyone on a moped can do that.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.720
<i>It's kind of like the Venus Line in 
Nagano that I drove down last year.</i>

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.590
<i>I feel like I'm driving in the sky.</i>

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.880
<i>Mom and Dad must have 
come through here, too.</i>

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:44.020
<i>It's really cold, but I'm glad I came.</i>

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:54.380
"See? I told you! 
We're lost in the mountains."

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:57.210
"Wait, was that a 'watch for deer' sign?"

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.020
"Deer?"

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.440
"There are deer here?"

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.960
Enough of the voice-over.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.410
It's been a while since we've seen Mt. Fuji!

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:19.220
Mt. Daruma Highland

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.920
<i>Geospot number ten: Mt. Daruma Highland.</i>

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:19.740
<i>A gentle highland formed from 
the eruption of Mt. Daruma.</i>

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:26.380
<i>The Nishiizu Skyline that traverses it 
is known as a tourist destination.</i>

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:30.130
Izu's so full of lookouts.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:33.110
We'd have to come here more 
than once to see everything.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:37.100
Seeing Mt. Fuji makes me feel 
like I'm getting close to home.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.730
It's weirdly calming.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.870
It must be because you've been to all sorts
 of places on your moped over the past year.

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:46.040
Hey, now, our Izu camp trip isn't over yet.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:46.900
Yeah!

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.530
We can't go home until we see the capybaras.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:51.630
You're right.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:55.640
Okay, girls, I've finished 
registering for the campsite.

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:57.130
Okay!

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.340
Well, let's get going.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:00.880
Let's get going!

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.410
<b>Daruma Forest 
Campsite</b>

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.160
<b>Daruma Forest 
Campsite</b>

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.190
You're starting dinner already?

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.520
Isn't it a bit early?

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:18.470
Well, the meal we're making 
is gonna take a few hours.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:21.530
It'll be late if we don't start early.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.230
I see.

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.280
What should we do, then?

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.180
W-Wanna visit the baths?

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.710
It's a little early, but...

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.040
The baths, huh?

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:36.300
Oh, right, Sensei picked up a hot 
spring pamphlet at reception.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.740
Shall we go, then?

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:39.190
You should go get warmed up.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.550
Exactly.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:42.550
Sensei, could you give us a... ride...

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.470
Midday drinking!

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.100
See you later!

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:54.820
Okay.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.330
Let's do this.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.580
The breeze is so nice.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.600
It feels great after a bath.

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:15.500
Cape Mihama

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:10.540
<i>Geospot number eleven: Cape Mihama.</i>

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.070
<i>A sand spit caused by coastal currents,</i>

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.500
<i>it also serves as a buffer 
against natural disasters.</i>

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:18.160
What a funny-shaped cape.

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:20.760
It's like a seawall.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:25.140
There's another cape ahead called 
Cape Ose, which looks similar.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.820
A lot of people get the two confused 
the first time they come here.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:32.640
That's the place Rin-chan 
was talking about yesterday.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.960
Akari-chan, what's wrong?

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.010
N-Nothing!

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:43.310
<i>We're going to be holding a mini 
birthday party for those two later.</i>

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.550
<i>Try to keep a casual eye on them, okay?</i>

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.860
<i>I can't let them catch on. 
It's supposed to be a surprise.</i>

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:55.180
Do you usually eat anything specific 
on your birthday, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:58.290
I guess my dad's beef stew.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:02.050
I can't wait to see what they make for us.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:05.870
You guys know we're having a birthday party?!

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:08.550
Of course we do. Aki was like...

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:12.480
Speaking of March, 
Inuko's birthday is on the fourth.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:14.570
Let's do something on our trip.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.190
So she said.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.510
Also, she was buying canned 
whipped cream earlier.

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:22.390
Those girls are so bad at surprises.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:27.410
Dinner is almost ready.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.820
Come on back.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:32.580
Sensei, dinner's ready.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.830
Shall we head back, then?

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:54.300
Happy birthday to you!

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.950
Happy birthday to you!

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:58.850
Inuko & Nadeshiko

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:03.700
Happy birthday, dear Inushiko!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.770
Happy birthday to you!

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:12.620
Okay, Aoi-chan, Nadeshiko-chan!

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.660
One, two...

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.980
Happy birthday!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.360
Now blow out <i>this</i> candle!

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.380
Not happening.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:34.390
<b>Inuko & Nadeshiko</b>

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:32.160
You made us a real cake and everything.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.390
Except it's pancakes inside.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.890
Also, these are for the two of you.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:41.050
You even got us presents?

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:41.880
We did.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.250
Can I open it?

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:47.390
Wooden cookware!

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:48.880
It's so fancy.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.410
This is what we saw at 
the Caribou in Fujiyoshida.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:55.830
It's made from a mix of tree resin and fibers.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.980
Apparently you can use it for hot drinks, 
and it's easy to care for.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:00.940
Wow.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.810
Thank you.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:05.260
I'll use it on our camping trips.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.050
I'll take good care of it.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:07.620
Yeah.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.670
Put them to good use.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:13.720
It's a bit embarrassing, having such 
a big celebration for our birthdays.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:15.680
Right?

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.620
Here we go.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.180
Okay!

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:23.090
Let's eat before it gets cold.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.880
Yeah, let's eat!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:28.630
Sensei, we have some snacks 
to go with your booze.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.700
<i>Wine and beer will go great with this!</i>

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:34.640
Yum!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:36.700
You can really taste the shrimp!

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:40.210
This shrimp and tomato risotto is so good.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.080
Yay!

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:46.170
We made the broth with the shell of 
the spiny lobster that Sensei bought us.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:48.590
And we used good cheese.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.840
Don't get too excited just yet.

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:55.260
Try it with some of the extra shrimp sauce.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:58.580
Shrimp!

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.910
The shrimpiness is so strong!

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.870
My whole mouth is shrimpy!

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.980
Shrimp everywhere!

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:06.860
Right?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.790
Can I try some?

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:13.860
Of course.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.870
<b>Ryouko</b>

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.870
Slide to answer

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:19.890
Hello?

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.570
<i>Hi, Onee-chan.</i>

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.870
<i>How are things going?</i>

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.370
We're having fun.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.330
Sounds like you aren't too drunk.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.130
<i>I told you I've been cutting back lately.</i>

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:32.650
<i>Good.</i>

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.170
<i>I'm glad you're doing a proper job as an advisor.</i>

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:38.180
I don't know about proper, but...

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:46.300
I wasn't too keen on being an advisor at first,

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:49.090
especially since it takes up a lot of time.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:56.720
But I'm getting to see my students 
grow up right before my eyes.

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:01.590
<i>And now I'm glad I accepted the job.</i>

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:07.600
<i>Maybe you just haven't run 
into any </i>real<i> problems yet.</i>

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:14.930
Well, make it back to 
Yamanashi safely, Sensei.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.370
<i>Yeah, yeah.</i>

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:19.800
<i>I'll bring the van home tomorrow 
evening along with some souvenirs.</i>

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:24.090
Hey, guys, want to watch the sun rise 
from Mt. Daruma tomorrow morning?

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:25.770
Yeah, let's do it!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:27.810
Should we go to bed early today, then?

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:48.330
Akari.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:49.720
We're here.

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.590
I changed my mind. I'm gonna sleep.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.620
It's cold. Close the door.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:57.840
Sheesh.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.810
I'll keep an eye on her.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.600
You girls go on ahead.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:12.120
Rin and Nadeshiko-chan are so fast.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.110
I thought the peak was right there...

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.570
It's so far!

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:25.530
It's like a dragon's back.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.270
So cold...

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.130
Mornings are cold in the mountains, huh?

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:34.880
Doesn't your face dry out when you bike?

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:39.630
My face got so dry when I was 
delivering New Year's cards.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.810
You can keep it moisturized with Vaseline.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:43.690
Vaseline?

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:48.320
Yeah, my mom taught me that 
you just need a thin layer.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.670
Of course...

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:54.720
Mom knew that because she used to bike, too.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:19:00.120
Oh, I just found out that my 
whole family used to ride.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.880
Your mom and dad, too?

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:02.780
Yeah.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:06.740
I guess your love of riding is in your genes, then.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:08.790
I guess that's how it goes.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:14.330
Here.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:17.800
It's instant, but it's spiny lobster miso soup.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:25.550
Warms you right up!

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:30.250
You can still taste the spiny lobster, 
even though this is the second time using it.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.310
Right?

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:37.140
We can dry and pulverize it to make 
powdered broth. It's still useful!

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.320
You're such a housewife.

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:45.660
We made it...

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.390
Oh, you're here!

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:48.980
The water's hot!

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.930
What a pick-me-up.

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:55.570
It's so warming.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:56.460
Wow.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:59.260
You can still taste the broth 
the second time around.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.220
Rin-chan said the same thing.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:07.030
It said 500 meters to the peak, 
so I wasn't expecting much,

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:08.750
but man, that was rough.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.680
It's 981 meters at the peak.

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:15.480
That's almost the same 
elevation as Lake Yamanaka.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.360
Wow, really?

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:20.440
We almost died in the cold at Lake Yamanaka.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.710
Seriously, though...

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.930
Thank you for your help that day.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:30.750
Uh, no, it was Sensei and Iida-san 
that actually saved you.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.620
We're going to Iida-san's place 
today to say thanks for the help.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.000
And to squish Choko-chan!

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.760
The sun's almost up!

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:06.550
What a nice view.

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.530
A sight for sore eyes.

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:18.150
All right, let's keep it up for our 
last day of Izu geospot touring!

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:18.820
Yeah.

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:20.260
And the capybaras.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.310
Capybara-chan...

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:35.260
Next Time

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:35.260
<b>We're Home</b>

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:41.260
<b>Plop</b>
